{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PeDJYQb2ReYJmtJgcFtPqu","type":"tool_result","content":"init | creates missing tasks/ and .taskspec/config\nsetup | none\nsetup signing | creates or explicitly rotates the repository-private HMAC key\ndemo | creates and removes an isolated temporary repository\nexample | writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\nExamples: task-plan, intent, recipe, incident, release-evidence. Use taskspec help example <kind>.\nnew | creates one Task-Spec scaffold and derived state\nplan | none\nbatch | creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\nmigrate | atomically upgrades one explicitly named legacy task under the task-state lock\nvalidate | refreshes deterministic derived state unless --no-state\ndod | none\ngate | --stamp writes the sign-off envelope; otherwise none\nhandoff | stdout is read-only; --out writes non-clobberingly unless --force\nrun | runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\naccept | --stamp atomically writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 plus the complete acceptance envelope\nauthor-doctor | none\nholdout | seal/run may write descriptor or receipt; verify is read-only\nreceipt | creator/sign commands write explicit receipt paths; validate is read-only\neval-audit | uses temporary git worktrees; optional report path\nidentity | init/sign/revoke write explicit files; verify is read-only\nevidence | run writes an explicit evidence directory; validate/plan are read-only\nbridge | export writes only with --out; validate is read-only\ndsse | export writes only to --out; verify is read-only\nmcp | read-only stdio server\nmesh | optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\nready | none\ngraph | none; TaskGraphView/v1 is derived from Markdown and Git\nstatus | none; emits TaskStatus/v1 and exactly one safe next command\nlint | none\ntransition | changes lifecycle status and derived state\nrebuild-state | rewrites deterministic tasks/_state.yaml\narchive | moves root done/parked tasks under the task-state lock and refreshes derived state\nbackup | writes a timestamped backlog archive to the selected destination\nmetrics | none\nconformance | self-test uses disposable fixtures only\nexecutor | reference L2 executor; transitions, executes, accepts, or parks one supplied task\nagent-context | none\ncompletion | none\ndoctor | none\nversion | none\nhelp | none\ndecompose | Native intent decomposition, signed topology review, and TaskPlan compilation.\nrecipe | Inspect and validate resolved bounded execution guidance.\nguide | Read version-matched installed workflow guidance.\ndecompose init | Create explicit intent workspace.\ndecompose prepare | Validate and project an authored recipe; never approve it.\ndecompose review | Authenticate explicit approval of the current topology.\ndecompose compile | Compile reviewed topology and lineage without sealing leaves.\ndecompose status | Explain planning blockers and next valid action.\ndecompose impact | Compare leaf projections to identify affected authorizations.\ndecompose import | Explicitly import originals; fresh native review required.\nrecipe list | List available pinned strategies.\nrecipe show | Show resolved guidance.\nrecipe validate | Validate a resolved recipe.\nsetup decompose | Provision locked dependencies in the private runtime.\nreceipt operational | Validate or import operational evidence without upgrading its trust.\nmesh init | Use the existing TaskMesh init operation.\nmesh doctor | Use the existing TaskMesh doctor operation.\nmesh serve | Use the existing TaskMesh serve operation.\nmesh frontier | Use the existing TaskMesh frontier operation.\nmesh run | Use the existing TaskMesh run operation.\nmesh status | Use the existing TaskMesh status operation.\nmesh watch | Use the existing TaskMesh watch operation.\nmesh explain | Use the existing TaskMesh explain operation.\nmesh cancel | Use the existing TaskMesh cancel operation.\nmesh resume | Use the existing TaskMesh resume operation.\nmesh accept | Use the existing TaskMesh accept operation.\nmesh finish | Use the existing TaskMesh finish operation.\nmesh adapters | Use the existing TaskMesh adapters operation.\nmesh setup | Use the existing TaskMesh setup operation.\nmesh mcp | Use the existing TaskMesh mcp operation.\nexample task-plan | Write the installed task-plan example; existing output requires explicit --force.\nexample intent | Write the installed intent example; existing output requires explicit --force.\nexample recipe | Write the installed recipe example; existing output requires explicit --force.\nexample incident | Write the installed incident example; existing output requires explicit --force.\nexample release-evidence | Write the installed release-evidence example; existing output requires explicit --force.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ceeea8b2-285a-465b-b497-8dff44bb5f61","uuid":"94a172fc-2407-44bb-96fd-1a34fd803e09","timestamp":"2026-09-14T22:07:30.771Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"init | creates missing tasks/ and .taskspec/config\nsetup | none\nsetup signing | creates or explicitly rotates the repository-private HMAC key\ndemo | creates and removes an isolated temporary repository\nexample | writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\nExamples: task-plan, intent, recipe, incident, release-evidence. Use taskspec help example <kind>.\nnew | creates one Task-Spec scaffold and derived state\nplan | none\nbatch | creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\nmigrate | atomically upgrades one explicitly named legacy task under the task-state lock\nvalidate | refreshes deterministic derived state unless --no-state\ndod | none\ngate | --stamp writes the sign-off envelope; otherwise none\nhandoff