{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L81Lau4rT4ccHnAnzssq6G","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Native decomposition and review\n2\t\n3\tUse `taskspec decompose prepare <id> --recipe <file>` to validate authored input\n4\tand propose topology. `--dry-run` produces diagnostics without changing the plan.\n5\tEach accepted seam owns one swimlane; each capability leg names an observable\n6\tstate and proof; executable leaves own coherent done-conditions and bounded writes.\n7\tSDLC stages are concerns on the work, not mandatory lanes.\n8\t\n9\tRead `tasks/.plans/<id>/delivery-plan.yaml`, proposed leg artifacts, and graph\n10\tbefore recording explicit human review:\n11\t\n12\t```bash\n13\ttaskspec decompose review <id> --accept --reviewer <identity> --reason <decision>\n14\ttaskspec decompose compile <id>\n15\ttaskspec plan --manifest tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\n16\ttaskspec batch --plan tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\n17\t```\n18\t\n19\tReview binds the complete topology through the repository HMAC key using the\n20\tplan-review domain. Compilation and materialization do not seal execution.\n21\tThe authored recipe, immutable snapshots, native TaskPlanLineage/v1, bundle,\n22\tand existing materialization receipt retain the intent-to-leaf chain.\n23\t\n24\tBefore replanning, preserve the prior bundle path. Use `prepare --replace`, review,\n25\tcompile, then `decompose impact <id> --against <prior-bundle.json>` to inspect\n26\tchanged, added, removed, and unchanged projections. Relevant constraints, recipe,\n27\tdependencies, proof, and source changes require renewed authorization. Unrelated\n28\tsibling changes preserve the earlier snapshot for unchanged leaves.\n29\t\n30\tRecipe task fields may include `execution_recipe` (a strategy name),\n31\t`shared_resources` (resource identifiers requiring serialization), and\n32\t`proves_capabilities` (leg IDs this integration-proof leaf independently evaluates).\n33\tAbsence of a proof leaf leaves a capability unproven even when all children are done.\n34\t\n35\tOptional `sdlc_stages` values are `plan`, `design`, `build`, `test`, `deploy`, and\n36\t`maintain`. One leaf may carry several concerns; these labels never create lanes\n37\tor replace required evals. Original intake text is retained in the review and\n38\tapplicable leaf constraints. Import rollback is tested before materialization.\n39\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ceeea8b2-285a-465b-b497-8dff44bb5f61","uuid":"074a9d87-2f5d-4abb-a641-f907f80a089b","timestamp":"2026-09-14T22:07:31.742Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat _zzwi1h9/.agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/decomposition.md","content":"# Native decomposition and review\n\nUse `taskspec decompose prepare <id> --recipe <file>` to validate authored input\nand propose topology. `--dry-run` produces diagnostics without changing the plan.\nEach accepted seam owns one swimlane; each capability leg names an observable\nstate and proof; executable leaves own coherent done-conditions and bounded writes.\nSDLC stages are concerns on the work, not mandatory lanes.\n\nRead `tasks/.plans/<id>/delivery-plan.yaml`, proposed leg artifacts, and graph\nbefore recording explicit human review:\n\n```bash\ntaskspec decompose review <id> --accept --reviewer <identity> --reason <decision>\ntaskspec decompose compile <id>\ntaskspec plan --manifest tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\ntaskspec batch --plan tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\n```\n\nReview binds the complete topology through the repository HMAC key using the\nplan-review domain. Compilation and materialization do not seal execution.\nThe authored recipe, immutable snapshots, native TaskPlanLineage/v1, bundle,\nand existing materialization receipt retain the intent-to-leaf chain.\n\nBefore replanning, preserve the prior bundle path. Use `prepare --replace`, review,\ncompile, then `decompose impact <id> --against <prior-bundle.json>` to inspect\nchanged, added, removed, and unchanged projections. Relevant constraints, recipe,\ndependencies, proof, and source changes require renewed authorization. Unrelated\nsibling changes preserve the earlier snapshot for unchanged leaves.\n\nRecipe task fields may include `execution_recipe` (a strategy name),\n`shared_resources` (resource identifiers requiring serialization), and\n`proves_capabilities` (leg IDs this integration-proof leaf independently evaluates).\nAbsence of a proof leaf leaves a capability unproven even when all children are done.\n\nOptional `sdlc_stages` values are `plan`, `design`, `build`, `test`, `deploy`, and\n`maintain`. One leaf may carry several concerns; these labels never create lanes\nor replace required evals. Original intake text is retained in the review and\napplicable leaf constraints. Import rollback is tested before materialization.\n","numLines":39,"startLine":1,"totalLines":39}}}
