{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf46QdRrXhbZMQbHznda1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything else is already recorded — one decision is missing.\n\n## Current state\n\n`taskspec decompose status rate-limit` → `DECOMPOSE=NEEDS_REVIEW`:\n- `plan_not_ready: Delivery plan is not marked ready.`\n- `review_missing: An accepted delivery-plan review is required.`\n\nPlanning artifacts are complete and self-consistent: seam map `SEAM_MAP=READY`, proposed graph `TASK_GRAPH=READY` with zero contentions, four seams → four swimlanes → four capability legs, and a linear critical path. No tasks have been materialized yet (`taskspec ready` is empty), so nothing is sealed or executing.\n\n## Already decided — I'm not re-asking these\n\n- **ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER** (`accepted`): the sequence is schema → effective policy → request-101 enforcement → visible reason + telemetry.\n- **OBJ-METERING-SEPARATION** (`FIXED`): provider-owned metering stays outside the four-leg proving path.\n- **Intent DI-RATE-LIMIT**: success criteria and out-of-scope items are recorded against blueprint evidence `E-BLUEPRINT`.\n\n## The one decision still missing\n\n**Your explicit approval of the proposed topology** — this is a human authorization the CLI will not synthesize, and it binds the whole topology through the repository HMAC key.\n\nThe topology you'd be approving:\n\n| Leg | Swimlane | Owner |\n|---|---|---|\n| LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID | LANE-POLICY-CONTRACT | platform-contracts |\n| LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED | LANE-POLICY-RESOLUTION | policy-runtime |\n| LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED | LANE-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT | request-runtime |\n| LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE | LANE-DECISION-VISIBILITY | reliability-interface |\n\nDependencies are strictly sequential: policy-schema → effective-policy → request-101 → decision-visibility.\n\nTo proceed I need two things from you:\n\n1. **Accept or object** to this four-lane split as it stands.\n2. If accepting: the **reviewer identity** to record and a **one-line reason** for the decision.\n\nThen the next command is exactly:\n\n```\ntaskspec decompose review rate-limit --accept --reviewer <name> --reason <reason>\n```\n\nNote that review is not a leaf seal — it unblocks `decompose compile` and `batch`, which create *unsealed* leaves. Authorizing their execution is a separate `gate --stamp` step later."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":882,"cache_read_input_tokens":27961,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":882},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ceeea8b2-285a-465b-b497-8dff44bb5f61","uuid":"fe989bad-7323-4c14-900d-673e4de0c135","timestamp":"2026-09-14T22:08:16.345Z","request_id":"req_011Cf46QcbFMAARUjt9knpgQ"}
